From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:09:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08534/11362] fix(arc): never-empty floor on discriminative
 frontier prune; memoize per-node frontier keys

Continues the 2026-08-08 adversarial live-agent review fix pass.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6225 (Correctness finding 3): the online-discriminator frontier
prune had no never-empty floor. A logistic discriminator fittable from as
few as 6 samples can transiently score every open-tier node below the 0.12
threshold, emptying `eligible`; `_frontier` then returns None and its
caller latches `explored_out = True` (assigned only at __init__, so the
latch never clears) -- the game ends with most of the action budget
unspent, reading as a legitimate "fully explored" null. Fixed by tracking
the highest-scoring pruned node and rescuing it instead of returning None,
mirroring the existing HazardMovePruner never-empty guard in this same
file. Genuine exhaustion (no open-tier nodes at all) is unaffected.

REQ-ARC-WMTE-6226 (Speed finding 2, shipped ON): `_frontier` recomputed two
expensive per-node keys from scratch on every call over immutable inputs --
the action-effect prior scores every untested candidate through the
frame-change scorer, and the goal-bias energy re-runs an exec'd Python
predicate on the node's frame. Fixed by caching both on the node dict
itself (mirroring the existing node["value"] lazy-cache pattern):
goal-bias score keyed on a new _goal_bias_generation counter (bumped only
by set_goal_bias, the sole post-construction mutator), action-effect key
keyed on len(untested) (which only ever shrinks, since
action_effect_expansion_prior is never replaced post-construction).

Tests: test_arc_frontier_never_empty_guard_20260808.py (5 tests),
test_arc_frontier_key_memoization_20260808.py (6 tests, using call-counting
stand-ins to prove cache hits, not just value equality). Broader sweep: 142
passed / 5 pre-existing environment skips across the frontier/goal-bias/
action-effect/discriminator/active-probe test areas.

Also acknowledges 12 results/ artifacts flagged stale by the artifact-
freshness-lint, reusing the same reachability arguments verified for the
immediately-prior 6223/6224 acknowledgement pass on this file (this fix
is confined to StepwiseExplorer methods none of these scripts reach live).

